  factText: "In forests, trees actually connect through mycelium. This underground
    \u201Cwood wide web\u201D lets trees swap nutrients and even signal each other
    to dangers. For example, birch and fir trees exchange carbon and water via these
    fungal links, showing plants cooperate underground for forest health."
